  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is RNA-only multiprofile with PCA and avgpool (config_002: 0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), showing that multiprofile aggregation is more useful than singleprofile or transformer aggregation for the current PCA representation. Image-only ResNet is weak, so the next clean extension is to test RNA representation within the best unimodal setting. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, isolating whether a learned nonlinear RNA representation improves on PCA. This is high-information under a limited budget: if it helps, it identifies a better RNA encoder for later multimodal tests; if not, PCA remains the preferred RNA representation."
}

